---
import SiteLayout from '@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { HOUSE_OPTIONS } from '@/lib/house-lookup';
import type { SeoMetadata } from '@/lib/seo';

const seo: SeoMetadata = {
  title: 'Astrology House Lookup: Understand the 12 Houses | NatalNode',
  description: 'Select one of the twelve astrological houses to explore its traditional interpretive themes in a focused educational lookup.',
  canonical: '/tools/house-lookup'
};
---

<SiteLayout seo={seo}>
  <main class="mx-auto w-[calc(100%-2rem)] max-w-5xl pb-16 pt-14 sm:pt-20">
    <header class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-natal-accent">Tools / House Lookup</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.04em] text-white sm:text-6xl">
        Explore an astrological house
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-natal-muted">
        Select one of the twelve numbered houses to explore its core domain, key themes, constructive expression, and balancing considerations.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-12 max-w-4xl rounded-2xl border border-natal-border bg-natal-surface/75 p-5 sm:p-8" aria-labelledby="house-selection-title">
      <div>
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-natal-accent">Make a selection</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-white" id="house-selection-title">
          Choose a numbered house
        </h2>
      </div>

      <form class="mt-6" data-house-lookup-form aria-describedby="house-lookup-boundary">
        <label class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-100" for="astrological-house">Astrological house</label>
        <select
          class="mt-2 block min-h-11 w-full max-w-md rounded-lg border border-natal-border bg-slate-950/40 px-3 py-2.5 text-sm text-white outline-none focus-visible:border-natal-accent focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-natal-accent"
          id="astrological-house"
          name="house"
          data-house-select
          required
        >
          <option value="">Choose a house</option>
          {HOUSE_OPTIONS.map((house) => <option value={house.id}>{house.label}</option>)}
        </select>

        <p class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-amber-200/20 bg-amber-200/5 p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300" id="house-lookup-boundary">
          This tool explains a house you select. It does not calculate house cusps or determine which house a planet occupies in a birth chart.
        </p>

        <button
          class="mt-5 inline-flex min-h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-natal-border px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-200 hover:border-natal-accent hover:text-white focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-natal-accent"
          type="reset"
        >
          Clear selection
        </button>
      </form>
    </section>

    <section
      class="mt-6 max-w-4xl rounded-2xl border border-natal-border bg-natal-surface/75 p-5 sm:p-8"
      data-house-result
      aria-live="polite"
      aria-labelledby="house-result-title"
      hidden
    >
      <div data-house-result-content></div>
    </section>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-natal-muted" data-house-empty role="status">
      Choose a numbered house to see a focused interpretation. No house is preselected.
    </p>
    <noscript>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-amber-100">
        JavaScript is required to generate the selected interpretation in this browser.
      </p>
    </noscript>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-10 border-t border-natal-border/70 pt-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <section aria-labelledby="what-houses-represent-title">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-natal-accent">What houses represent</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-white" id="what-houses-represent-title">
          Context for chart themes
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-natal-muted">
          Within astrology’s interpretive framework, houses describe areas of life or experience where a chart theme may be considered. They are not physical places and they do not determine a person’s choices. This lookup provides a compact vocabulary for reflection, separate from the calculation of any chart.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="house-sequence-title">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-natal-accent">How the twelve houses differ</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-white" id="house-sequence-title">
          A sequence of domains
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-natal-muted">
          The twelve houses form a sequence of related but distinct domains, from identity and self-direction through private reflection. In a full chart, a house supplies context for a planet or sign; the house itself is not a prediction. Choose a number above to focus on one domain at a time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="birth-time-title">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-natal-accent">Why birth time can matter</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-white" id="birth-time-title">
          House calculation is a separate task
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-natal-muted">
          In an actual natal chart, house cusps and planet-house placements can depend on birth time, birth location, and the chosen house system. If the exact birth time is unknown, exact house-based claims should not be assumed. This page collects none of that information and does not calculate cusps, angles, or placements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="how-to-use-title">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-natal-accent">How to use the lookup</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-white" id="how-to-use-title">
          Read the result as a starting point
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-natal-muted">
          Choose a house, read its core domain and key themes, then consider the constructive expression and balancing consideration together. The language is educational and symbolic. You can continue with the <a class="text-natal-accent underline decoration-natal-accent/50 underline-offset-4 hover:text-white" href="/tools/sign-lookup">Sign Lookup</a> or <a class="text-natal-accent underline decoration-natal-accent/50 underline-offset-4 hover:text-white" href="/tools/aspect-lookup">Aspect Lookup</a> for related vocabulary.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="lg:col-span-2" aria-labelledby="calculation-disclosure-title">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-natal-accent">House meaning vs calculation</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-white" id="calculation-disclosure-title">
          An explanation, not a house calculator
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-natal-muted">
          Different house systems can place cusps or planets differently, but this lookup does not select, compare, or calculate a house system. Terms such as maintenance, shared resources, transition, privacy, and less-visible processes are interpretive prompts; they are not medical diagnoses, financial predictions, death predictions, or psychiatric labels. For more context on chart inputs, read <a class="text-natal-accent underline decoration-natal-accent/50 underline-offset-4 hover:text-white" href="/learn/what-is-a-natal-chart">What Is a Natal Chart?</a> or return to the <a class="text-natal-accent underline decoration-natal-accent/50 underline-offset-4 hover:text-white" href="/tools/">Tools hub</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>

<script>
  import { initializeHouseLookup } from '@/lib/house-lookup';

  initializeHouseLookup();
</script>
